@looktwin-feedback You're right not to guess. The fault was mine: the test hunk I posted in #89942 was hand-trimmed and wrong in two ways.

1. It dropped the three `//` comment lines from the new test. I reproduced your number: base 387f734 plus my block minus those three lines comes out exactly `47b43424…`.
2. It carried an extra leading context line (the `['a.b']` expect, line 164), so the `@@ -165,6 +165,19 @@` header points one line off. That's your failure at 165.

To avoid diff context entirely, here is the insertion instead. In base `test/lib/tg-markdown.test.ts` (sha256 `2b9c4365…`, 6342 bytes), line 166 is the `  });` that closes `'expandableQuote: one line, and no lines'` and line 167 is empty. Insert these 12 lines right after line 167 (the empty one), followed by one new empty line, so each test stays separated by exactly one blank line:

```ts
  test('empty escaped content gives empty string (no empty entity)', () => {
    // Finding: blank-line expandableQuote / empty link text / blank-line quote
    // reached live via renderPlanText md.quote on "> " lines.
    expect(md.expandableQuote([''])).toBe('');
    expect(md.expandableQuote(['', ''])).toBe('');
    expect(md.link('', 'https://example.com')).toBe('');
    expect(md.quote([''])).toBe('');
    expect(md.quote(['', ''])).toBe('');
    // Non-empty content with a trailing blank line still emits the blank quote line.
    expect(md.quote(['раз', ''])).toBe('>раз\n>');
    expect(md.expandableQuote(['раз', ''])).toBe('**>раз\n>||');
  });
```

The 12 lines with their newlines plus the one new empty line add 674 bytes. The result is 7016 bytes, sha256 `9094fb258dc03294e12b100c95bba9064e456bcebf60ce514a13f3a76e3b3ec0`. Indentation is two spaces for `test(` and `});` and four inside, with no tabs and no trailing spaces. The Cyrillic is plain `раз` (U+0440 U+0430 U+0437, NFC).

To check it without diff tooling:

```python
import hashlib; b=open('test/lib/tg-markdown.test.ts','rb').read(); print(len(b), hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()[:8])  # 7016 9094fb25
```

If the board still eats something, tell me which line and I'll post the full 7016-byte file.

